#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147305 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4487c2b9-b681-5e1d-a2d9-c3231afcf03d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Laplace Transform of a Second-Order ODE"}] :question/id #uuid "8165df56-763a-5f36-9e21-9ed7b0e50190" :question/math-academy-id "e-6663" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y(t)\\right\\}$ for $s\\geq\\sqrt5$ if\n$y'' - 5y = 4e^{-3t}, \\quad y(0)=2, \\quad y'(0)=-1$." :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{y^{″} - 5y} &= L{4e^{-3t}} \\\\\nL{y^{″}} - 5L{y} &= 4L{e^{-3t}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwe use the formula for the Laplace transform of a second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y\\right\\}-sy(0)-y'(0)=s^2Y(s)-sy(0)-y'(0)\n$$\n\nTaking into account the given initial conditions, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{y''\\right\\}=s^2Y(s)-2s+1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{e^{-3t}\\right\\}=\\dfrac{1}{s+3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL{y^{″}} - 5L{y} &= 4L{e^{-3t}} \\\\\n(s^{2}Y(s) - 2s + 1) - 5Y(s) &= \\frac{4}{s + 3} \\\\\n(s^{2} - 5)Y(s) &= \\frac{4}{s + 3} + 2s - 1 \\\\\n(s^{2} - 5)Y(s) &= (4 + (2s - 1)(s + 3))/(s + 3) \\\\\n(s^{2} - 5)Y(s) &= \\frac{2s^{2} + 5s + 1}{s + 3} \\\\\nY(s) &= (2s^{2} + 5s + 1)/((s + 3)(s^{2} - 5))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147306 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d5c275-af4a-5bdd-a97c-c937824d8e94" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order Initial Value Problem Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/id #uuid "cfc54894-5add-5272-bf47-6495f5f4d288" :question/math-academy-id "e-6666" :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ if the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n$y'' + 6y = 2\\sin {2t}, \\quad y(0) = 0, \\quad y'(0) = 2$\n\nis given by\n\n$s^2Y(s) - 2 +6 Y(s) = 2\\left(\\dfrac{2}{s^2 + 4}\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns^{2}Y(s) - 2 + 6Y(s) &= 2(\\frac{2}{s^{2} + 4}), \\\\\n(s^{2} + 6)Y(s) &= 2 + \\frac{4}{s^{2} + 4} \\\\\n(s^{2} + 6)Y(s) &= \\frac{2s^{2} + 12}{s^{2} + 4} \\\\\n(s^{2} + 6)Y(s) &= (2(s^{2} + 6))/(s^{2} + 4) \\\\\nY(s) &= \\frac{2}{s^{2} + 4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\nL{\\sin 2t} = \\frac{2}{s^{2} + 4}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL^{-1}{Y(s)} &= L^{-1}{\\frac{2}{s^{2} + 4}} \\\\\ny(t) &= \\sin 2t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\ny(t) = \\sin {2t}\n$$\n\nis the solution of the original differential equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "30d5c275-af4a-5bdd-a97c-c937824d8e94" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Second-Order Initial Value Problem Using Laplace Transforms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "63dda1e1-8662-5806-b64a-1b69adf9ec00" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186144407}] :question/id #uuid "ccd487bf-6852-5287-bce6-d2a3cbfbcf1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-345071" :question/problem "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n$y^{″}(t) - y(t) =-2\\sin t, y(0) = 0, y^{′}(0) = 1$\n\nis given by\n\n$s^{2}Y(s) - 1 - Y(s) =-2(\\frac{1}{s^{2} + 1})$.\n\nThe solution is $y(t) =$\n{{field-1}}"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4487c2b9-b681-5e1d-a2d9-c3231afcf03d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Laplace Transform of a Second-Order ODE"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "897207a6-74c9-5b48-9b4a-9bb235c75ae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s) = \\frac{s^{3}}{s^{2} - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146612} {:answer/id #uuid "08c45fea-d01e-54c6-8590-a6e99283a22a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s) = (2)/(s^{3}(s^{2} - 2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146613} {:answer/id #uuid "1c41d678-c725-5706-a166-de4ec42fe0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s) = (2(s^{3} + 1))/(s^{3}(s^{2} - 2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146614} {:answer/id #uuid "36aa0458-b76f-56ae-a844-1b9ffa70ae88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s) = (s^{3} + 1)/(s(s^{2} - 2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146615} {:answer/id #uuid "64a99644-be90-5807-866e-4bbf5fc86fc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s) = (2(s^{3} + 2))/(s^{3}(s^{2} - 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c41d678-c725-5706-a166-de4ec42fe0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Y(s) = (2(s^{3} + 1))/(s^{3}(s^{2} - 2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146614} :answer-field/id #uuid "42280dc8-87b7-523b-a6ea-fba592c104d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146611}] :question/id #uuid "e3ffd082-96ac-58ad-b713-c48e243a1029" :question/math-academy-id "q-64442" :question/problem "Find the Laplace transform $Y(s) = L{y(t)}$ for $s \\ge \\sqrt{2}$ if\n\n$y^{″} - 2y = t^{2}, y(0) = 0, y^{′}(0) = 2$."}]}
